%N A397264 Number of rooted binary simplex time-consistent leaf-labeled galled trees with n leaves and exactly 1 gall.
%H A397264 Lily Agranat-Tamir, Michael Fuchs, Bernhard Gittenberger, Noah A. Rosenberg, and Karthik V. Seetharaman, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aam.2026.103131">Combinatorial comparison of general galled trees, time-consistent galled trees, and simplex time-consistent galled trees</a>, Adv. Appl. Math. 180, 103131 (2026). See the g=1 column of Table 4.
%F A397264 E.g.f.: -x*(x+sqrt(1-2*x)-1)/(1-2*x)^(3/2) (see Agranat-Tamir et al. 2026, eq. 56).
%e A397264 For n=3 leaves, there are 3 rooted binary simplex time-consistent leaf-labeled galled trees with a root gall from which three leaves are descended, one each for the three distinct labels for the single leaf that descends from the reticulation node. Hence, a(3)=3.
%Y A397264 Cf. A398145 for rooted binary simplex time-consistent leaf-labeled galled trees with n leaves and no constraints on the number of galls.
%K A397264 nonn
%O A397264 0,4
%A A397264 _Noah A Rosenberg_, Jul 22 2026
